{
  "version": 1,
  "checked": "2026-11-13",
  "about": "Cloud speech-to-text providers shared by the desktop app (include_str!), Android (core resources) and Chrome (JSON import + manifest CSP). Every request fact below was checked against the provider's official docs on the date above; entries with experimental=true have at least one fact the docs did not confirm (see notes). Placeholders: {model}, {region}, {id} (job id), {file} (uploaded file id). max_seconds is the per-request cap (the lower of the provider's duration limit and its upload size limit at 32 kB per second of 16 kHz mono 16-bit WAV); longer recordings are split at quiet points and the texts joined. live: the provider's streaming WebSocket (see docs/research/cloud-integration.md): url/query/lang, native header auth (live.auth or auth), browser short-lived token (never the key in a URL), start/ready, audio (binary pcm_s16le at rate, or a JSON template with {audio} base64), messages (match -> partial|delta|final|tokens|result|error|done), join, end ({seq} = audio frames sent), end_done. live.map: the chosen batch model -> its live counterpart; otherwise a batch model that is also a live model is kept, else live.default_model.",
